  date         = {2020},
  eprint       = {1911.02508},
  eprinttype   = {arxiv},
  urldate      = {2026-09-05},
  note         = {Read arXiv:1911.02508v2 (2020-02-03) in full for chapter 14 on 2026-09-05, all 7 pages, fetched from arXiv rather than from the corpus folder because this paper is not in the corpus (decision 34's second use). Two revisions exist and the book cites v2. arXiv's own record carries no journal-ref and no Comments field, so arXiv says nothing about where this was published; the PDF's own first page carries the ACM reference block for AIES '20 with publisher DOI 10.1145/3375627.3375830. That is decision 53's case, so the book cites the arXiv version and the venue stays in this note. Read for the scaffolding construction, the out-of-distribution detector it routes on, the three datasets, the shift rates, the fidelity of the adversarial classifier to the biased one, and the hyperparameter sweep that shows the attack does not depend on any LIME or SHAP setting. Every number chapter 14 prints from it is anchored in research/ch14-giai-thich-duoi-tan-cong.md.},
}

